Note that Magicbane must be wielded to give MR.  Eventually it'd be
nice to wield Excalibur again, go check the castle for any possible
scales that the dragons dropped.

The Castle is the level just before the Valley of the Dead (the Valley
is the top level in Gehennom, with an altar to Moloch and a bunch of
graveyards).  There is always a wand of wishing in a chest in one of
the four towers at the corner of the castle.

Also check the castle armory for potential cloak of magic resistance,
etc before using up those wishes.

Read the wishing spoiler carefully and be sure that unless you have a
scroll of charging (and a way to bless it) your first wish from the
wand goes for 2 or 3 blessed scrolls of charging.

Make sure you identify the wand before zapping it, and don't zap it at
0:0 but you can wrest out a last charge at 1:0.

For the future:
1. Both liches and mind flayers respect Elbereth, so if you have a way
to reliably engrave it they should never get more than one attack in (h
should never get any if you're careful).
2. Magicbane is a reliable way to engrave E in one turn, as are wands
of digging and fire.  Lightning too but it can blind you.
Fire/lightning are permanent, digging/magicbane aren't but they last a
lot longer than writing in the dust with your fingers.

